WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.900 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A lot of pundits,

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
some people
who are already running

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.770 line:92%
are warning about this idea

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
that if the Democratic Party
goes too far left,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.309 line:92%
that will enable a Trump victory

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
because people in the center
will flee to him

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.847 size:88% position:44% line:92%
out of fear of the left.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I strongly disagree
with that.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:19.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think one of the reasons
that people like Trump

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
get elected is so many
working people

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
and lower income people
have given up

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the political process
and they don't vote.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.361
And compared to other countries
around the world,

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
our voter turnout is not
particularly high.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think what we need
are candidates

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.303
who speak to ordinary people
who today are in a lot of pain.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right?
We don't talk about it enough.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got mothers all over
this country

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:45.045
who cannot find quality
childcare for their little ones.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:48.415
We have kids who are graduating
college

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.650 line:92%
$40,000, $50,000, $100,000 debt.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
Others can't even afford
to go to college.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got people who work in
two or three jobs

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
while we have the
three wealthiest people

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this country owning
more wealth

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.828 size:84% position:42%
than the bottom half
of the American people.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got to raise that
as a moral issue.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we have so many people
in poverty,

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.935 line:92%
so many people uninsured,

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.104 line:92%
is it acceptable that so few

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
have so much money
and so much power?

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.308
And I think when you start
talking about those issues

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:18.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you say, "Yeah,
I understand you can't make it

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.145 size:75% position:38% line:92%
on 10 bucks an hour.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:22.715
I understand that you're worried
about the future generation,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.818
worried about whether your kids
are gonna have

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lower standard of living
than you have.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're worried about
climate change."

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.891
When we speak to the needs
of working people and we say,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:35.295
"Yes. We are prepared to take on
Wall Street

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.896 line:92%
and the fossil fuel industry

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all of the big money
interests

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
to create an economy
that works for all of us."

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.870
I think people say,
"You know what? It's about time,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.871 line:92%
and I'm gonna go out and vote,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.873 size:78% position:39%
and I'm gonna support
those candidates."

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's my view.
-You had a --

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
there were so many things

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
about your last campaign
that were successful,

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
but ultimately you didn't win
the nomination.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.716
One thing that people reflecting
back would say

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.419
is that you did not have
a diverse enough coalition

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.387 size:78% position:39% line:92%
of people behind you.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
How have you addressed that
moving into this?

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a very fair question.
We ended up --

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, one of the problems
with the last campaign

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:11.531
is when we began, you know,
I come from a very small state.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was not known
by a whole lot of people.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.235 line:92%
But as the campaign progressed,

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:18.705
we did much better with
the African-American community,

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:22.408
with the Latino community,
and we did better in general.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
And by the time
the campaign ended,

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.046
what I'm really excited about --
we want to build on --

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:30.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that we ended up getting
more votes

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
from young people,
black, and white, and Latino,

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.922 line:92%
Asian American, Native American,

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.691 line:92%
than Clinton or Trump combined.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.160 line:92%
That's pretty good. Okay?

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, what we --
but your point is right.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:47.167
You know, we started off
with a few people from Vermont,

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the campaign
moved so quickly.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did not put together
the kind of diverse campaign

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.942 size:81% position:41%
that we should have,
and this time we will,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:56.809 size:81% position:41% line:92%
in fact, do just that.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm glad to hear that.
I heard you say, you know,

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
one thing you might do
is obviously you're running,

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.551 size:81% position:41%
as you've established,
a pathological liar,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:07.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we try to establish
every night.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:07.720 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.723
I've heard the joke you're gonna
bring a lie detector onstage,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a debate.
But in reality,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
how do you run against
someone who --

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:15.695 line:92%
Obviously, you're very left.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
You must be aware that Donald
Trump would paint you

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:20.099
as even farther left than that.
-You know, Seth, here's the --

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
I never use the word left.
-Yup.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't -- I am.
I'm a Democratic socialist.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.271 line:92%
So, that's the way it is.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the issues
that we talk about,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it left to say that
in this country

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
we should have minimum wage
that is a living wage?

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:35.448
Is it left to say that everybody
should have healthcare

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:38.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a right, that we should
expand Social Security?

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because so many of our people
can't make it --

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:44.324
elderly people can't make it
on $12,000, $13,000 a year.

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:47.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it left to say
that we have to rebuild

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.094 line:92%
our crumbling infrastructure

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
and create millions
and millions of jobs?

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:53.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it left to say we have
to address

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.467 line:92%
the crisis of climate change

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:57.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
or that we have to deal
with criminal justice reform

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.371 size:81% position:41% line:92%
or immigration reform?

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have to deal with sexism,
racism, and homophobia.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think
those are left issues.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I think sometimes
the media

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:05.878 line:92%
makes a bigger deal about it.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.482
I think, in fact,
on all of those issues and more,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.085 line:92%
sensible gun safety legislation.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you have
the strong majority

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:17.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the American people saying,
"Yeah, I agree with that."

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
And let's have people in
Washington who stand with me

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.429 size:88% position:44%
rather than just wealthy
campaign contributors.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's kind of what
this campaign is about.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.635 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You obviously
have a very good job.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.007 size:81% position:41%
You're trying to get
another very good job,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you also had
some other jobs.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:39.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
We found a clip.
You were in a movie in 1988.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:39.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
A real movie. A real movie.
-Oh, no.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to get going here.
-No, no, no.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:43.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's called
"Sweet Hearts Dance."

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:47.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
A real cast, Jeff Daniels,
Susan Sarandon.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.589
-Susan, yeah.
-How do you end up in this film?

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should notice --
your character's name

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:52.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
is Bernie.
-Yes.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you playing yourself?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.696
-It wasn't that we did a lot
of auditioning for the film.

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:57.230 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:02.368
it happened to be that the film
was shot in Vermont.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.103 line:92%
That helped. And they went --

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was Mayor of the city
of Burlington.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.741
We helped them out getting some
extras and so forth and so on.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.743
So I said, "Hey,
I'm a good extra. I'll do that."

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
That was about it.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:15.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we actually have --
we have a clip,

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.216 line:92%
and I really think you're great.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's take a look at Senator
Sanders here

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "Sweet Hearts Dance."
-My acting career.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi.
-Trick or treat.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How you doing?
-Trick or treat, Bernie.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Trick or treat.
-Trick or treat.

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Come on, Bernie.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fill them up there.
-Okay, here you go.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.063 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-And let me just say --

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:30.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.898 line:92%
-Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.600 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think -- I think
that's an Oscar award.

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That was fantastic.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-I think it was great.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:43.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think that --
I really like that the clip

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:46.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you distributing out candy
fairly.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Free candy.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:48.281 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Free. Right, absolutely.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.016 size:81% position:41%
-No one should have to
pay for their candy.

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:54.253
Give it up for Senator
Bernie Sanders, everyone.

